:"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73396.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73396.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"With `use_task_logical_date=True`, `BranchDayOfWeekOperator` and `BranchDateTimeOperator` crash when task context supplies neither `logical_date` nor a Dag run. This change gives users an error that tells them which date information is missing, following the existing `DayOfWeekSensor` behavior.\n\nFor example, calling `choose_branch(context={})` previously raised `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'run_after'`. It now raises `ValueError` with this message:\n\n> Either `logical_date` or `run_after` should be provided in the task context when `use_task_logical_date` is True\n\nContexts that provide a logical date or a Dag run's `run_after` keep their existing branch behavior.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Added `test_choose_branch_should_raise_when_neither_logical_date_nor_run_after` to `test_weekday.py` and `test_datetime.py`. Earlier validation recorded in this PR verified both fail on the old code and pass with the fix.\n- Earlier Breeze validation recorded in this PR: both full operator test files passed (58 passed), with Ruff lint and formatting checks passing on all touched files.\n- Hosted checks on head `4def4ad7ce08348e93f0edd6cadaa710f5f9c11f`: 142 successful, 12 skipped, and CodeQL neutral; no failed or pending checks.\n- This maintenance pass did not rerun local tests or validate a standalone task execution environment.\n\nFixes #72031\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [X] Yes (Muse Spark (Meta); OpenAI Codex (GPT-6))\n\nGenerated-by: Muse Spark (Meta); OpenAI Codex (GPT-6) following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\n\n---\n\n* Read the **[Pull Request Guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#pull-request-guidelines)** 